{\xe \v glfwInit\:Initialization, version and error reference}
{\xe \v Initialization, version and error reference\:glfwInit}
\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid {
{\b 
{\b GLFWAPI} int glfwInit ({\b void} )}}
\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAABAIJ}
{\bkmkend AAAAAABAIJ}
{
\pard\plain \s61\li360\sa60\sb30\qj\widctlpar\qj\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
\par
{
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Initializes the GLFW library. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This function initializes the GLFW library. Before most GLFW functions can be used, GLFW must be initialized, and before an application terminates GLFW should be terminated in order to free any resources allocated during or after initialization.\par
If this function fails, it calls {\b glfwTerminate} before returning. If it succeeds, you should call {\b glfwTerminate} before the application exits.\par
Additional calls to this function after successful initialization but before termination will return {\f2 GLFW_TRUE}  immediately.\par
The {\b GLFW_PLATFORM} init hint controls which platforms are considered during initialization. This also depends on which platforms the library was compiled to support.\par
{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
Returns\par}\pard\plain \s82\li720\widctlpar\ql\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\s17 \sa60 \sb30
{\f2 GLFW_TRUE}  if successful, or {\f2 GLFW_FALSE}  if an error occurred.\par
}}@errors Possible errors include {\b GLFW_PLATFORM_UNAVAILABLE} and {\b GLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR}.\par
{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
Remarks\par}\pard\plain \s82\li720\widctlpar\ql\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\s17 \sa60 \sb30
@macos This function will change the current directory of the application to the {\f2 Contents/Resources}  subdirectory of the application's bundle, if present. This can be disabled with the {\b GLFW_COCOA_CHDIR_RESOURCES} init hint.\par
@macos This function will create the main menu and dock icon for the application. If GLFW finds a {\f2 MainMenu.nib}  it is loaded and assumed to contain a menu bar. Otherwise a minimal menu bar is created manually with common commands like Hide, Quit and About. The About entry opens a minimal about dialog with information from the application's bundle. The menu bar and dock icon can be disabled entirely with the {\b GLFW_COCOA_MENUBAR} init hint.\par
{\b Wayland, X11:}  If the library was compiled with support for both Wayland and X11, and the {\b GLFW_PLATFORM} init hint is set to {\f2 GLFW_ANY_PLATFORM} , the {\f2 XDG_SESSION_TYPE}  environment variable affects which platform is picked. If the environment variable is not set, or is set to something other than {\f2 wayland}  or {\f2 x11} , the regular detection mechanism will be used instead.\par
@x11 This function will set the {\f2 LC_CTYPE}  category of the application locale according to the current environment if that category is still "C". This is because the "C" locale breaks Unicode text input.\par
}}@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread.\par
{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
See also\par}\pard\plain \s82\li720\widctlpar\ql\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\s17 \sa60 \sb30
intro_init \par
{\b glfwInitHint} \par
{\b glfwInitAllocator} \par
{\b glfwTerminate}\par
}}{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
Since\par}\pard\plain \s82\li720\widctlpar\ql\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\s17 \sa60 \sb30
Added in version 1.0. \par
}}}}
