\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAABAIO}
{\bkmkend AAAAAABAIO}
{
\pard\plain \s61\li360\sa60\sb30\qj\widctlpar\qj\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
\par
{
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Terminates the GLFW library. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This function destroys all remaining windows and cursors, restores any modified gamma ramps and frees any other allocated resources. Once this function is called, you must again call {\b glfwInit} successfully before you will be able to use most GLFW functions.\par
If GLFW has been successfully initialized, this function should be called before the application exits. If initialization fails, there is no need to call this function, as it is called by {\b glfwInit} before it returns failure.\par
This function has no effect if GLFW is not initialized.\par
@errors Possible errors include {\b GLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR}.\par
{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
